   Multikey Index
A Multikey Index is an index that MongoDB creates on a field whose value is an array.
Simple Definition
A Multikey Index is an index used to efficiently query fields that contain arrays. MongoDB creates index entries for the individual elements of the array.
{
    name: "Laptop",
    brand: "Dell",
    tags: ["electronics", "computer", "laptop"]
}
db.products.createIndex({
    tags: 1
})

db.products.find({
    tags: "bestseller"
}).explain("executionStats")

Text Index
A Text Index in MongoDB is an index designed to efficiently search for words or phrases inside string fields.
Simple Definition
A Text Index allows MongoDB to perform text searches on string content, such as searching for specific words in product descriptions, articles, reviews, or comments.

db.products.find({  
      description: 'This is a high quality Clothing product from HP with excellent features and performance.'
}).explain("executionStats")

db.products.createIndex({
    description: "text"
})
db.products.find({
    $text: {
        $search: "Samsung"
    }
}).explain("executionStats")

Hashed Index in MongoDB
A Hashed Index is an index where MongoDB stores a hash value of the indexed field instead of the field's original value.
Simple Definition
A Hashed Index uses a hash function to generate a hash value for a field and is mainly useful for equality-based queries and distributing data evenly across shards.
db.products.createIndex({
    productId: "hashed"
})
db.products.getIndexes()
db. products.find({
    productId: 101
})

Geospatial Index in MongoDB
A Geospatial Index in MongoDB is an index used to efficiently store and search location-based data, such as latitude/longitude coordinates.
Simple Definition
A Geospatial Index allows MongoDB to efficiently perform queries based on geographical locations, such as finding nearby restaurants, shops, hospitals, or calculating distances between locations.
location: {
    type: "Point",
    coordinates: [longitude, latitude]
}
